'' '-g' DESCRIBES VARIABLES AND THEIR TYPES, not only lines. Before, the compile unit was
'' LineTablesOnly and a debugger stopped in a tiko program saw no variable at all --
'' lldb's "no variable information is available in debug info for this compile unit".
''
'' Every assertion is a node shape clang 21 emits for the same C construct, and the
'' program was run under LLVM 21's lldb on Windows ('-debug:dwarf' PE) with every value
'' compared against the same program built by fbc: the parameters by reference and by
'' value, the string descriptor showing "Hello", the UDTs, the enum as 'Green', the
'' fixed and dynamic arrays, the bitfields reading 5 and 17 (fbc's unsigned reading),
'' the base type as inheritance, the static local and the shared globals.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -g --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/debug-vars.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' The compile unit is full debug info, and it lists the globals.
'' EXPECT-OUT: emissionKind: FullDebug, globals: !{
'' A local's home is its alloca, declared once for the whole procedure.
'' The intrinsic, not LLVM 19's #dbg_declare record, so clang 18 reads it (T67).
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void @llvm.dbg.declare(metadata ptr %s
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DILocalVariable(name: "MyLong"
'' Names keep the DECLARED spelling -- identifiers intern folded -- and a parameter is
'' numbered.
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DILocalVariable(name: "ByRefArg", arg: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_reference_type
'' A STRING is its descriptor; a dynamic array its FBARRAY, 'data' typed.
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_structure_type, name: "string"
'' EXPECT-OUT: name: "FBARRAY(long)"
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_enumeration_type, name: "Colour"
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DIEnumerator(name: "Green", value: 2)
'' EXPECT-OUT: DIFlagBitField
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_inheritance
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_union_type, name: "Pun"
'' A fixed array keeps its declared bounds.
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DISubrange(count: 3, lowerBound: 1)
'' A wide character is 'wchar_t', or lldb shows a 'wstring * N' as numbers.
'' EXPECT-OUT: name: "wchar_t", size: 16
'' A scalar is a typedef with FreeBASIC's name: lldb re-spells a basic type in C.
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_typedef, name: "integer"
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DIGlobalVariable(name: "ShCount"
'' A static local is a global scoped to its procedure.
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DIGlobalVariable(name: "CallCount"
'' A procedure is named by its source spelling, with no linkage name to override it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DISubprogram(name: "Show", scope:
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DISubroutineType(types: !{null,
'' ...and one in a procedure that is never emitted still has a subprogram to be scoped
'' to: 24 corpus files were 'use of undefined metadata' under '-g' until it did.
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DIGlobalVariable(name: "Hidden"
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DISubprogram(name: "NeverCalled", scope:
'' A declared array is named as FreeBASIC declares it -- lldb numbers from 0 and DAP has
'' no bounds, so the name is where a debugger front end reads them -- and a fixed-length
'' string likewise, so a NUL-terminated buffer can be told from a space-padded one.
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_typedef, name: "long(1 to 3)"
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_typedef, name: "short(0 to 1, 0 to 2)"
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_typedef, name: "zstring * 8"
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_typedef, name: "string * 5"
'' EXPECT-OUT: DW_TAG_typedef, name: "wstring * 8"
'' EXPECT-OUT: name: "FBARRAY(long)"
'' The file is named with its directory, as clang does: an attaching debugger has no
'' launch directory to resolve a bare name against.
'' EXPECT-OUT: !DIFile(filename: "debug-vars.bas", directory: "
'' EXPECT-NOT: directory: "")
